n be written in expanded form as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =⋯+1000{d}_{4}+100{d}_{3}+10{d}_{2}+{d}_{1} \\\\  & =100(⋯+10{d}_{4}+{d}_{3})+10{d}_{2}+{d}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the residue of $a$ modulo $100:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & ≡100(⋯+10{d}_{4}+{d}_{3})+10{d}_{2}+{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,100) \\\\  & ≡0\\cdot (⋯+10{d}_{4}+{d}_{3})+10{d}_{2}+{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,100) \\\\  & ≡0+10{d}_{2}+{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,100) \\\\  & ≡10{d}_{2}+{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,100)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $10{d}_{2}+{d}_{1}$ is the two-digit number consisting of the last two digits of $a.$\n\nFinally, since $b=215a,$ and \n\n$$\n215≡15\\,(\\text{mod}\\,100)\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & ≡10{d}_{2}+{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,100) \\\\ 215a & ≡10{d}_{2}+{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,100) \\\\ 15a & ≡10{d}_{2}+{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,100)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression that gives the last digit of $215a$ is the following:\n\n$$\n15a\\,\\text{mod}\\,100\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4dc1d3c2-ea95-5409-b806-aa17c7b0cff8" "answer-field-fec96176-6e4b-5b1f-af15-6a4b4b87e54e" "answer-field-739873ae-7222-56d4-a75e-62dfb4f6ff56"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4dc1d3c2-ea95-5409-b806-aa17c7b0cff8" :answer-field/id #uuid "4dc1d3c2-ea95-5409-b806-aa17c7b0cff8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-92f1412d-1f75-560e-a351-03c9164622a4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-92f1412d-1f75-560e-a351-03c9164622a4" "answer-effeb510-969c-5a3f-85d4-ec87567c869b" "answer-0fe8e591-ad12-52f4-a2f8-1bca3dfd6296" "answer-96b46831-8183-5119-84cc-89942ba3993e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92f1412d-1f75-560e-a351-03c9164622a4" :answer/id #uuid "92f1412d-1f75-560e-a351-03c9164622a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15a" :db/ensure [:answer/v